From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:21:22 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Descriptor skip window that does not kill the title;
 coalesced refreshes; readable-range copies

tabled_lately leaves a slot to its draws for 240 frames without asking whether a draw read it through a table. A slot the title stops reading through a table keeps being skipped, and a draw that reads it directly gets a record no pass made: the title dies at victory-image+0x23cf683 (write 0x0), reproducibly, at world entry (frames 2112/2253/2573 on this box). VICTORY_TABLED_SKIP_FRAMES=<n> asks the stricter question (read through a table within n frames); =2 gave two clean runs through the world where the shipped window gave three crashes. Unset keeps today's behaviour.

Batch::flush coalesced 25,000-90,000 refreshes of 11-21 KB a frame into 24,000-50,000 calls: ranges of one copy within 64 KB become one, and Shadow::update still cuts the merged range around what shaders write.

VICTORY_COPY_FAST=1 (off by default): copy_mapped moves a range the kernel reports readable with memcpy (700-1,300 MB/s measured) instead of ReadProcessMemory (600 MB/s). Off until the unmap race has a guarded copy.

watch::forgot resets the write-watch bits the layer's own write-back sets.

Measured on i7-12700F/16 GB/RTX 3080: 2885 ms -> 1261-1376 ms a frame in the world (0.35 -> 0.73-0.79 fps), loading 232 s -> 84 s.
